            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>UN Partition Plan of 1947</strong><br>\nIn 1947, the United Nations proposed a plan to divide Palestine into a Jewish and an Arab state. The plan was accepted by Jewish leaders but rejected by Arab leaders. This led to further tensions and conflicts between the two communities in the region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Foundation of the State of Israel</strong><br>\nOn May 14, 1948, David Ben-Gurion, the first Prime Minister of Israel, declared the independence of the Jewish state. This led to the outbreak of the first Arab-Israeli war, in which multiple Arab states intervened. The war ended in a ceasefire, but the borders and the status of Palestine remained disputed.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Six-Day Wars and Beyond</strong><br>\nIn 1967, the escalation of tensions led to the Six-Day War, during which Israel gained control over additional territories, including the West Bank and the Gaza Strip. In the subsequent decades, there have been several more conflicts and peace efforts, yet a definitive solution to the conflict remains elusive.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
