          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Oslo Accords</strong><br>\nIn 1993 and 1995, the Oslo Accords were signed between Israel and the Palestine Liberation Organization (PLO), providing for temporary self-administration for the Palestinians in parts of the West Bank and the Gaza Strip. However, the accords did not lead to a lasting peace solution, and violence flared up again in the following years.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Current Situation</strong><br>\nThe present situation is characterized by ongoing tensions and periodic outbreaks of violence. Both sides have deeply rooted claims to the land, and efforts towards a two-state solution have repeatedly failed. The unrest and conflicts have led to a tragic loss of human lives and enduring mistrust between the communities.</p>\n\n<p><strong>International Efforts</strong><br>\nThe international community, including the United Nations and other international organizations, has repeatedly tried to mediate in the conflict and find a solution. Despite some progress, a lasting and just solution for both sides remains a challenging and unresolved task.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3d655444-fd55-42f7-aba2-16a16db7dc58"
